<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63623" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῐτᾰν-εύω</span></b> , in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λλ</span> in augm. tenses, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλλιτάνευε, ἐλλιτάνευσα</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιτανός</span>): —<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pray, entreat</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντας δ᾽
				ἐλλιτάνευε</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δὲ λ.</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.422
			</span></i>:— Constr. same as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίσσομαι</span>, either abs., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.145
			</span></i>: or c. acc. pers., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				9.581
			</span></i>, etc.; that by which one prays in gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γούνων ἐλλιτάνευσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.481
				</span></i>
			; for which in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.357
			</span></i> we have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ἄγε, γούνων
				ἁψάμενοι λιτανεύσομεν</span> (
				Ep.
			 for -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωμεν</span>); also c.
				inf., <i><span class="en">
				23.196
			</span></i>: c. acc. pers. et inf., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				469
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				8.8
			</span></i>, etc.: c. Adj. neut., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ λ. τινά</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.32
			</span></i>: rare in 
				Att.
			 Poets, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				49
			</span></i> (dub. l.), and in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.4.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				388b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ps.</u>
				44(45).12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. τὸ θεῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					15.1.60
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς θεοὺς εὐχαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					4.76
				</span></i>
			.</div>
